@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix semapv: <https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/> .

# Term equivalences for the colourspace domain — GMEOW authoring source.
# Compiled to mappings/gmeow-colourspace.sssom.tsv by `gmeow compile-mappings`.
#
# No mature, widely-adopted RDF/OWL colourspace ontology exists. ICC profiles are
# binary file formats; CSS Color Module is a rendering spec; ONVIF provides only
# XML namespace strings for colourspace attributes. GMEOW therefore mints its own
# seed ReferenceFrame individuals (sRGB, CMYK) and uses frameSolver to point to
# authoritative procedural specs by reference (Principle 12).

# REFUSED (Principle 5 — no faithful external term):
#   No external ontology provides a rigorous conceptual model of colourspace as
#   a reference system. GMEOW retains colourspace frames as canonical terms
#   without alignment rather than force weak matches.
# REFUSED (Principle 5):
#   gmeow:FrameRealm, gmeow:FrameKind, gmeow:Axis have no colourspace-specific
#   external counterparts.

gmeow:mapsetColourspace a gmeow:MappingSet ;
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-colourspace.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:setId "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/mappings/colourspace" ;
    gmeow:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    gmeow:setComment "Colourspace alignments. No mature target ontology exists; this mapping set is intentionally minimal, documenting the gap. Seed frames (sRGB, CMYK) are canonical GMEOW terms with frameSolver references to ICC specifications." .
